<title>ITALY: Italy's airport workers to strike on June 25.</title>
<headline>Italy's airport workers to strike on June 25.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian airport workers unions said on Friday they would stage a national strike on June 25, the latest stoppage in a protracted dispute over working conditions and job cuts.</p>
<p>Air transport unions said in a statement that the four-hour strike would begin at 10 a.m. (0800 GMT).</p>
<p>A strike by air traffic controllers was called off earlier this month after the government and the unions reached a last minute accord. Local public transport, trains and taxi unions have also called strikes this year.</p>
